{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-17472","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15633","text":"[&] Protocol — Agent Skills"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-17474","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15634","marks":["bold"],"text":"Purpose:"},{"id":"spn-15635","text":" Teach any LLM or developer how to use the [&] Protocol correctly, idiomatically, and in the right sequence. These files cover everything from writing your first agent declaration to building providers that satisfy capability contracts."}]}],"id":"blk-17473","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-17475","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15636","text":"Quick Orientation"}]},{"id":"blk-17476","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15637","text":"The [&] Protocol is a "},{"id":"spn-15638","marks":["bold"],"text":"language-agnostic specification for capability composition in AI agents"},{"id":"spn-15639","text":". It defines how agents declare cognitive capabilities ("},{"id":"spn-15640","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory"},{"id":"spn-15641","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15642","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason"},{"id":"spn-15643","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15644","marks":["code"],"text":"&time"},{"id":"spn-15645","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15646","marks":["code"],"text":"&space"},{"id":"spn-15647","text":"), how those compose via "},{"id":"spn-15648","marks":["code"],"text":"&"},{"id":"spn-15649","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-15650","marks":["code"],"text":"|>"},{"id":"spn-15651","text":" operators, and how declarations compile into MCP and A2A configurations."}]},{"id":"blk-17477","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15652","text":"[&] sits at the "},{"id":"spn-15653","marks":["bold"],"text":"composition layer"},{"id":"spn-15654","text":" of the agent protocol stack — above MCP (agent-to-tool) and A2A (agent-to-agent). It does not replace either protocol. It generates configurations for both."}]},{"id":"blk-17478","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15655","text":"The Core Workflow"}]},{"id":"blk-1